.TH WAVE-UPGRADE 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-upgrade \- Upgrade a package to its latest version; with --all, every installed package. Old versions are kept — -X, --remove-old-versions removes them in the same run.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave upgrade <package> | wave upgrade \-\-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upgrade a package to its latest version; with --all, every installed
package. Old versions are kept — -X, --remove-old-versions removes them
in the same run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Upgrade every installed package that has a newer version
.TP
.B \-X, \-\-remove\-old\-versions
Remove the older versions as part of the upgrade
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-continue
Resume an interrupted download
.TP
.B \-\-proxy <string>
HTTP/HTTPS proxy (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080)
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-ssl
Skip SSL certificate verification (insecure)
.TP
.B \-\-limit\-rate <string>
Limit download speed (e.g. 200K, 1M, 5M; a bare number means bytes)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-time <string>
Maximum total time for one request (40s, 1min, 1min20s, 2h; a bare
number means seconds)
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-timeout <string>
Maximum time for the handshake
.TP
.B \-\-content\-time <string>
Maximum time to receive data
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-force
Install anyway when the running macOS is older than the package declares
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Verbose mode

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave upgrade jq
wave upgrade jq -X
wave upgrade --all
wave upgrade jq --remove-old-versions --max-time=2min
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
